## Problem

Users had to manually write 145+ lines of MSW handlers for each CRUD endpoint. Request was for auto-mocking all API endpoints at startup from a simple configuration.

## Changes

### Auto-Handler Generation
- **`src/mocks/createMockHandlers.ts`**: Generates MSW handlers from object metadata (discovery, meta, CRUD endpoints)
- **`objectstack.config.ts`**: Declarative data model definition
- **`src/mocks/browser.ts`**: Reduced from 145 to 40 lines (72% reduction)

### Implementation

**Before:**
```typescript
// Manual handlers for each endpoint (145 lines)
const handlers = [
  http.get('/api/v1/data/task', ({ request }) => {
    const url = new URL(request.url);
    const top = parseInt(url.searchParams.get('$top') || '100');
    const tasks = Array.from(mockTasks.values());
    // ... 20 more lines
  }),
  http.post('/api/v1/data/task', async ({ request }) => {
    // ... 15 more lines
  }),
  // ... 5 more endpoints
];
```

**After:**
```typescript
// Auto-generated from config (40 lines)
export async function startMockServer() {
  seedData('task', [/* initial data */]);
  const metadata = { objects: appConfig.objects.reduce(...) };
  const handlers = createMockHandlers('/api/v1', metadata);
  const worker = setupWorker(...handlers);
  await worker.start({ onUnhandledRequest: 'bypass' });
}
```

### Technical Details
- Handles client path compatibility (`/api/v1` and `/api/v1/api/v1`)
- In-memory Map-based storage with auto-ID generation
- Supports all standard ObjectStack endpoints (discovery, meta, CRUD)

## Result

![Working Application](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/140a897b-39e1-4fe2-80a9-fa1cf4335b70)

All CRUD operations verified: Create (201), Read (200), Update, Delete working with auto-generated handlers from single config file.

